        "original_id": "a485e99c-c70c-5fb2-941c-84dbed7ced95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: LD Beghtol, Damian Costilla\n- Bands: Flare Acoustic Arts League, The Magnetic Fields, The Smiths, Love, The Velvet Underground\n- Albums: 69 Love Songs\n- Companies: Merge Records\n- Places: Fort Campbell, Kentucky, New York\n- Roles: musician, art director, writer, guitarist, singer\n- Topics: experimental pop, indie pop, musical influences, collaboration\n\nFacts:\n- LD Beghtol was born in 1964 in Fort Campbell, Kentucky.\n- LD Beghtol is an American musician, art director, and writer.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League, also known as Flare, was formed in New York in 1996 by guitarist Damian Costilla and singer LD Beghtol.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was an experimental pop band known for intense, darkly romantic, atmospheric songs.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was influenced by The Smiths, The Magnetic Fields, Love, various 4AD bands, and The Velvet Underground.\n- LD Beghtol sometimes collaborated with The Magnetic Fields.\n- 69 Love Songs is the sixth studio album by the American indie pop band The Magnetic Fields.\n- Merge Records released 69 Love Songs on September 7, 1999.",
